{
  "name": "Commercial cleaning: work one territory a week from a sheet of postal codes",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Commercial cleaning: work one territory a week from a sheet of postal codes\n\n### How it works\nGrow route by route. Your sheet lists postal codes with a radius in miles. Every Monday the workflow takes the first row without a status, counts facility managers, property managers, office managers and building managers based within that radius, and saves them as a list named after the territory. If the count fits max_per_week, the list goes into your campaign and the row is marked done with the count; if not, the row is marked too large so you can split it. Only valid emails join the campaign.\n\nCosts: counting is free; adding costs 1 credit per new person.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Create a sheet with the columns postal_code, radius_miles, status, people and add your territories.\n4. Pick it in **Next open territory** and **Mark the territory**, and pick the campaign.\n5. Set max_per_week in **Settings** and activate.\n\n### Customization\nChange the job titles in **Count managers nearby** for other buyers, such as hotel or clinic managers.",
        "height": 626,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "12acf7a3-7654-44e6-91eb-f040d1f2eaa3",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -360
      ]
    },
